---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const description = "Understand the L1 baseline, what your scan report contains, and how Insidia tests its own scanner.";
---
<Base title="Benchmark | Insidia Labs" description={description} path="/benchmark">
  <Header />
  <main id="content" class="wrap" style="padding:3rem 0 4rem">
    <p class="kicker">Coverage and results</p>
    <h1>Understand what your scan checked.</h1>
    <p class="lede">A useful result shows the checks that ran, the findings they produced, and anything left untested. Start with the L1 baseline and review the coverage in your report.</p>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>Start with the baseline</h2>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>L1 baseline</h3>
        <p>Run <code>insidia scan --policy L1</code> for baseline checks without a model. This is the default policy in a new configuration. L2 and L3 are not available yet.</p>
        <p>Review skipped checks as well as findings. A check that could not run does not count as a pass. See <a href="/docs/concepts/what-it-tests/">current coverage</a> for supported checks and limitations.</p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>Review and share your results</h2>
      <p><code>insidia scan --policy L1</code> writes a directory under <code>.insidia/runs/</code>:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><code>benchmark.json</code> — policy name, pass or fail, control results, and skips</li>
        <li><code>findings.json</code> — each finding names its engine, probe, severity, and taxonomy</li>
        <li><code>results.sarif</code> — for code scanning in CI</li>
        <li><code>report.html</code> — one file, opened with <code>insidia report --open</code></li>
      </ul>
      <p>The report includes mappings to supported OWASP frameworks where available. Use them to organize your review, together with the evidence and coverage for that run.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>How we test Insidia</h2>
      <p>The repository includes test apps with known vulnerabilities. We use them to check scanner behavior and catch regressions. Results on those apps do not establish detection accuracy on your application; use your own scan's evidence and coverage when reviewing a result.</p>
      <p><a href="https://github.com/Rushi-Balapure/Insidia-Labs/tree/main/benchmark">Read the benchmark directory</a> · <a href="/#install">Install the CLI</a></p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
